        <h3 class="font-bold text-ink text-base mb-1">
          1. Hydrodynamic Shearing &amp; Micro-Cavitation Clump Declustering
        </h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted">
          In opaque food suspensions (cloudy orange juice, liquid whole egg, oat milk emulsions), target bacterial endospores (such as <em>Alicyclobacillus acidoterrestris</em> and <em>Bacillus cereus</em>) naturally agglomerate into clumps or hide behind suspended pulp fibers and fat globules (30–120 µm). Conventional UV light fails because suspended solids attenuate UV photons within less than 0.1 mm according to the Beer-Lambert law (I = I_0 · exp(-α · c · z)). 
          Dynamic High-Pressure Homogenization (DHPH / UHPH) forces the fluid at 100–300 MPa through micro-metric polycrystalline diamond or zirconia orifices (gap δ = 4–10 µm). The instantaneous fluid velocity exceeds 400 m/s, producing extreme dynamic shear rates (γ̇ = v / δ &gt; 10⁷ s⁻¹), localized elongational stress, and intense acoustic cavitation (P_collapse &gt; 1.2 GPa). This nanosizes suspended particles to d32 &lt; 0.4 µm, declusters bacterial aggregates, and subjects microbial cell coats to sub-lethal permeabilizing tension without significant macroscopic heat rise (ΔT &lt; 4.0°C).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="border-l-2 border-sky-500 pl-4 py-1">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-ink text-base mb-1">
          2. Photobiological Pyrimidine Dimerization &amp; High-Peak Xenon Pulsed UV-C
        </h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted">
          Immediately downstream of the homogenization micro-gap, the declustered fluid enters an annular turbulent quartz reactor. High-intensity pulsed light (PUVC) generated by xenon flash tubes delivers broad-spectrum radiation (200–1100 nm) with 45–54% of radiant energy concentrated in the germicidal UV-C band (200–280 nm). Unlike continuous low-pressure mercury lamps that deliver continuous low irradiance (10–50 mW/cm²), pulsed xenon delivers peak irradiances exceeding 2,000 W/cm² in ultra-short microsecond pulses (100–300 µs). 
          Photons striking exposed microbial endospores cross-link adjacent thymine and cytosine bases in DNA/RNA, generating cyclobutane pyrimidine dimers (CPDs) and pyrimidine (6-4) pyrimidone photoproducts. The instantaneous high photon density saturates enzymatic photoreactivation and Nucleotide Excision Repair (NER) systems, inducing lethal double-strand DNA breakage and irreversible spore inactivation.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="border-l-2 border-emerald-500 pl-4 py-1">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-ink text-base mb-1">
          3. Annular Thin-Film Fluid Mechanics &amp; Secondary Vortex Mixing
        </h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted">
          To achieve complete lethality in high-absorbance fluids, the reactor constrains fluid flow into an ultra-thin annular gap (δ_gap = 0.25–0.50 mm) around high-purity synthetic Suprasil quartz sleeves. The annular geometry is designed to maintain fully developed turbulent flow (Re = ρ · v · D_h / µ &gt; 4,500) with secondary Dean vortices induced by helical ribbing:
        </p>
        <div class="bg-surface-soft p-3 rounded-xl border border-hairline my-2 font-mono text-xs text-ink overflow-x-auto">
          De = Re · (D_h / 2R_c)^(0.5) &gt; 120
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted">
          These helical secondary vortices continuously sweep fluid elements from the dark outer wall to the illuminated quartz boundary layer, ensuring every cubic millimeter of fluid receives the critical threshold radiant dose (F_crit ≥ 22.0 J/cm²) without laminar dead zones or shadowing.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="border-l-2 border-amber-500 pl-4 py-1">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-ink text-base mb-1">
          4. Synergistic Inactivation Modeling (Geeraerd-Van Impe &amp; Weibull Kinetics)
        </h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted">
          The coupled inactivation of bacterial endospores exceeds the algebraic sum of individual DHPH and PUVC treatments due to true mechanistic synergism:
        </p>
        <div class="bg-surface-soft p-3 rounded-xl border border-hairline my-2 font-mono text-xs text-ink overflow-x-auto">
          Log10(N0 / N)_synergy = Log10(N0 / N)_DHPH + Log10(N0 / N)_PUVC + Φ_synergy · [ (P / P_ref) · (F / F_ref) ]^0.65
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted">
          Where Φ_synergy ≈ 1.8–2.4 represents the synergistic multiplier resulting from mechanical spore coat thinning and unmasking prior to photonic irradiation. In liquid whole egg, temperature remains strictly below 25°C, preventing ovalbumin and conalbumin denaturation (T_coag &gt; 58°C) and providing 100% fresh functional foaming and culinary properties.
        </p>
      </div>
